WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.120
The ninth installment of the "The Fast and the&nbsp;
Furious" franchise is racing toward the finish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.160
line and onto the big screen. The latest movie in&nbsp;
the high-octane series was released in Hong Kong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.680
South Korea, and Russia in May 2021, and soon the&nbsp;
rest of the world will be able to join in on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.000
gasoline-scented action and thrills of "F9." The&nbsp;
film broke records at the box office, debuting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.080
at $163 million in its international opening, and&nbsp;
with earnings now over $6 billion worldwide. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.720
those numbers, it doesn't look like the movie&nbsp;
will be stepping on the brakes anytime soon.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.920
The "Fast and Furious" movies have&nbsp;
been on track for 20 years now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.200
and the newest film promises more wild stunts&nbsp;
and heart-pounding chases than ever before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.880
"F9" sees the return of director Justin&nbsp;
Lin, who previously helmed the "Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.680
and Furious" films 3 through 6. Here's&nbsp;
everything we know about the film so far.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.640
The "F9" movie has been in limbo for nearly two&nbsp;
years, with various delays causing the film to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.520
be pushed back several times. The initial plan&nbsp;
would have seen "F9" in theaters back in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.080
summer of 2019, but that release date was put on&nbsp;
hold to make room for the release of the buddy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.520
comedy spin-off, "Hobbs and Shaw." Universal, the&nbsp;
film's distributor, then made plans for a May 2020&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.720
release, but had to push things back once again&nbsp;
because of the pandemic. At last, the wait for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:23.840
American audiences will soon be over, as "F9"&nbsp;
finally releases State-side on June 25, 2021.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.000
Now that the U.S. has seen a surge of&nbsp;
vaccinations to fight off the coronavirus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.160
film studios are optimistic that more audiences&nbsp;
will be flocking to theaters this summer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.120
With many public places reopening and lifting&nbsp;
many of their restrictions, Universal is hoping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.480
that "F9" will be as big of a box office&nbsp;
smash in the States as it has been overseas.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.360
"Fast and Furious" fans are no doubt eager to&nbsp;
see the return of their favorite characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.720
in the long-awaited sequel, and they will not&nbsp;
be disappointed. Franchise veteran Vin Diesel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.600
leads the cast of "F9," reprising his role as&nbsp;
protagonist Dominic Toretto. Dominic has come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.520
a long way from the first film in the series&nbsp;
— from leading his own gang of criminals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:07.520
to becoming a fugitive on the run, to graduating&nbsp;
to a kind of high-profile, gray-market mercenary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.920
tasked with taking down some of the most&nbsp;
dangerous crime lords around the world.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.160
"You got&nbsp;
the best crew in the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.840
standing right in front of you.&nbsp;
Give 'em a reason to stay."

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.600
Michelle Rodriguez returns as Letty Ortiz,&nbsp;
the tough-as-nails mechanic and the love of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.320
Dominic's life. Letty and Dom have been through a&nbsp;
lot together over the years, from Letty's supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.680
death to her amnesia, and the ultimate return of&nbsp;
her memories. If their history is anything to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.920
by, it's unlikely that the couple will have&nbsp;
much time to themselves in the newest film.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.920
Also returning for "F9" are Tyrese Gibson as Roman&nbsp;
Pearce, Chris "Ludacris" Bridges as Tej Parker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.080
Jordana Brewster as Mia Toretto, and&nbsp;
Lucas Black as Tokyo Drift's Sean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.840
Boswell. A notable addition to the cast is, of&nbsp;
course, John Cena, who will play Jakob Toretto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.120
Dom's long-lost brother, who has become a&nbsp;
master thief and assassin. Charlize Theron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.640
will return as cyberterrorist Cipher, teaming&nbsp;
up as the co-antagonist alongside Cena's Jakob.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.400
The official summary for "F9" promises&nbsp;
multiple settings in "F9," and has the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.960
crew trotting around the globe in the newest film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.800
London, Tokyo, and Edinburgh are just&nbsp;
a few of the locations mentioned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.480
along with Central America and the scenic capital&nbsp;
of Tbilisi, Georgia. The summary also reads:

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:27.040
"Along the way, old friends will be resurrected,&nbsp;
old foes will return, history will be rewritten,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.360
and the true meaning of family&nbsp;
will be tested like never before."

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.840
Also of note: The "Furious" crew will&nbsp;
finally be heading into outer space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.160
because of course they will.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.680
Long time "Fast and Furious" fans&nbsp;
know how much family means to Dom.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.160
"I don't got friends. I got family."

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.040
Although we don't know much&nbsp;
about Jakob at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.200
there is certain to be plenty of conflict&nbsp;
as Dom goes up against his long-lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.840
brother — and seeing him team up with one&nbsp;
of Dom's most dangerous foes from the past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.520
is sure to pile on the drama. And, of&nbsp;
course, most importantly, Han is back:

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.040
"Nice clubhouse."

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.320
We can't wait to see how Dom and his crew take on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.240
this newest set of challenges when&nbsp;
"F9" finally arrives in the U.S.

